module

public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter13.Section08.ComponentSieve.AlternatingAndLinear.FourStructure.ChiefFactors.Basic

/-!
# The permutation-module input for the dual lower-bound route

In 13.8.25 the marked subgroup `(H ∩ M)* = (L₁T)*` is the stabilizer
of a two-dimensional subspace of the natural four-space. By 13.8.4(5),
`V_H/U_H` is generated by the orbit of the image of `V/V₃`, which this
parabolic fixes pointwise. The predicate below records exactly this linear
consequence, using the same actor identification in both the parabolic and
the representation. It asserts no exclusion of transvections.

A proof that such a representation has no displacement of rank one would
supply the second alternative in 13.8.11(1), hence the strict actor inclusion
used by `DualLowerBound`. That intrinsic exclusion remains a separate
obligation; a permutation-module label alone does not establish it.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, combined
manuscript (1 March 2004), 13.8.4(5), printed p.947; 13.8.11(1), p.950;
and the identification of `L₁T` in 13.8.25, pp.960–962.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter13.Section08.ComponentSieve.AlternatingAndLinear.FourStructure.CriticalTransfer.PairConsequences

variable {K V : Type*} [Group K] [AddCommGroup V] [Module (ZMod 2) V]

/-- The concrete generating-vector property of a quotient of the permutation
module on the cosets of a plane parabolic. The vector is allowed to vanish,
so the zero quotient is included. -/
def IsPlaneParabolicGenerated (τ : Representation (ZMod 2) K V)
    (eK : K ≃* BinaryLinear.GL ChiefFactors.NaturalSpace) : Prop :=
  ∃ (P : Submodule (ZMod 2) ChiefFactors.NaturalSpace) (v : V),
    Module.finrank (ZMod 2) P = 2 ∧
      (∀ g, eK g ∈ BinaryLinear.parabolic P → τ g v = v) ∧
      Submodule.span (ZMod 2) (Set.range (fun g => τ g v)) = ⊤

end CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter13.Section08.ComponentSieve.AlternatingAndLinear.FourStructure.CriticalTransfer.PairConsequences
